commit 1848099f063e99d4ffecbd7667766d54862398b9
Author: Mark Wielaard <mark@klomp.org>
Date:   Fri Sep 18 00:24:34 2026 +0200

    stdlib: Don't call clearenv from __libc_setenv_freemem
    
    Since commit 7a61e7f557a9 ("stdlib: Make getenv thread-safe in more
    cases") clearenv doesn't call any deallocation functions anymore.
    __libc_setenv_freemem (called from __libc_freeres) now clears all
    backing arrays. So there is no reason anymore to call clearenv from
    __libc_setenv_freemem.
    
    Tested against valgrind memcheck with --run-libc-freeres=yes which is
    the default.
    
    Reviewed-by: Florian Weimer <fweimer@redhat.com>
    (cherry picked from commit b837aae83df8fe80c8977b5ed5c538aebd2b152a)

